2026-04-30 18:10:32,025 - [36mDEBUG[0m agent_orchestrator - {"message": "Getting filler text: result", "tool_filler": "Please hold while I check this. ", "call_id": "call_simulation_5fd074c", "tool_obj": {"name": "execute_code", "description": "Execute sandboxed Python EXCLUSIVELY for computing payment plan amounts, validating payment schedules and expiry dates. DO NOT use for any text processing, parsing, matching, or verification tasks.\\n\\nUSE ONLY FOR:\\n- Computing installment amounts (e.g., divide $1200 into 4 monthly payments)\\n- Calculating down payments, remaining balances, payment splits\\n- Verifying if a payment schedule meets guidelines (e.g., is $200/month above minimum threshold of $150?)\\n- Generating payment due dates from a start date and frequency\\n- Computing fees, interest, or percentages applied to payment amounts\\n- Checking if deferral period falls within allowed date range\\n- Checking if the card stays valid and does not expire before the last payment date for a payment plan\\n- Credit card number parsing - use tol to validate length of the card\\nNEVER USE FOR:\\n- Date of birth verification, parsing, or comparison - handle conversationally\\n- Phone number verification, parsing, or formatting - handle conversationally\\n- Name matching or comparison - handle conversationally\\n- Social Security number verification or parsing - handle conversationally\\n- Address parsing - handle conversationally\\n- Any text/string comparison or matching - handle conversationally\\n- Converting spoken numbers to digits (e.g., \"one zero five\" to 105) - handle conversationally\\n- Account number verification - handle conversationally\\n\\nRule: If the task involves COMPARING or VERIFYING user-provided information against stored data (names, DOBs, phone numbers, etc.), DO NOT use this tool. Only use for CALCULATING payment amounts and schedules.\\n\\nTool Notes:\\n- Print only final numeric result; no intermediate output\\n- Ultra-concise: <=3 lines, single expression preferred\\n- NO COMMENTS: Do not include any comments in the code. Write self-explanatory variable names if needed, but never use # comments\\n- For money: use Decimal, quantize to 2 decimals with ROUND_DOWN\\n- Default timezone: US/Eastern", "parameters": [{"name": "code", "description": "Python code for payment calculations only. Write clean, readable Python across multiple lines as needed. Use proper line breaks between statements - do NOT use semicolons to chain statements. NO COMMENTS allowed. Example:\nfrom decimal import Decimal\ndebt = Decimal('1250.00')\ndown = Decimal('250.00')\ninstallments = 4\nmonthly = ((debt - down) / installments).quantize(Decimal('0.01'))\nprint(monthly)", "type": "string", "required": true, "items": null}], "filler_text": "Just a moment please. "}, "tool_filler_type": "<class 'str'>"} [90m{"call_id": "call_simulation_5fd074c", "room_name": null, "tenant_id": null} [90m/Users/vansh/Developer/agent-orchestrator/agent_orchestrator/proagent/state_loop.py:397[0m

